### What was the specific geographic location or address of the trash can labeled "Ballot Box" in Philadelphia?
Answer: According to the search result, the trash cans with the "Ballot Box" signs were located "at Broad and Sansom Streets and 15th and Sansom Streets" in Philadelphia.

Source URL: https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/election-2020-ballot-box-trash-can-ad-philadelphia-union-league-foundation-20201023.html

### Who placed the "Ballot Box" sign on the trash can in Philadelphia?
Answer: The "Ballot Box" sign was placed on the trash can by the Union League Legacy Foundation as "an advertisement... for the Union League Legacy Foundation’s exhibit on the history of voting rights."

Source URL: https://www.inquirer.com/politics/election/election-2020-ballot-box-trash-can-ad-philadelphia-union-league-foundation-20201023.html

### Was the "Ballot Box" sign on the Philadelphia trash can part of an official city initiative, an artistic installation, a prank, or a deliberate act of voter suppression?
Answer: The "Ballot Box" sign on the Philadelphia trash can was not an official city initiative, an artistic installation, a prank, or a deliberate act of voter suppression; rather, it was an "unfortunate advertising blunder" by the Union League Legacy Foundation to promote its exhibit on the history of voting rights, titled "Ballot Box: America’s Fight for the Vote." The foundation's chief administrative officer stated that the misleading signage "was certainly not intended" to confuse voters, and the advertisements were quickly removed once the mistake was realized.

