Answer: Yes, local authorities responded to the incident after receiving "at least one complaint to the District Attorney’s Election Task Force." The task force instructed the foundation to remove the advertisements immediately, and the city's "Streets Department deployed sanitation workers to sort through the trash of those bins... looking for any ballots a voter may have slipped in."

